<h1>Tattoo Aftercare Guide</h1>
<p class="muted">Heal it right and your ink stays bold for decades. Here's the routine real artists swear by.</p>

<h2>The first 48 hours</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Leave the initial wrap on for the time your artist tells you (usually 2–24 hours).</li>
  <li>Wash gently with lukewarm water and fragrance-free soap. Pat dry — never rub.</li>
  <li>Apply a thin layer of aftercare balm or ointment. Thin is key: too much suffocates the skin.</li>
  <li>Keep it clean, keep it moisturized, and keep it out of the sun.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Weeks 1–3</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Moisturize 2–3 times a day as the tattoo peels and flakes. Don't pick the flakes.</li>
  <li>No soaking — showers only, no baths, pools, or hot tubs for at least 2 weeks.</li>
  <li>No direct sun on the fresh tattoo. After it's healed, sunscreen keeps the colors from fading.</li>
</ul>

